# Local test configuration for Notation Prettifier.
#
# The corpus run reads real notes through this file, so no personal path or
# document name is ever committed. Copy it to .testenv and fill in your own
# values:
#
#   cp .testenv.example .testenv
#
# .testenv is gitignored and never leaves your machine. A key that is left
# blank means its checks are skipped with a notice; a key that is set but
# points at nothing stops the run, so a typo is noticed instead of ignored.

# A folder of real notes to run the corpus checks against. The run bakes every
# .md file in it, checks idempotency, delimiter and brace balance, and renders
# a sample through the reading view. It never writes to the folder.
NP_TEST_FOLDER=

# Extra privacy patterns for test/privacy.mjs: a comma separated list of
# regular expressions that must never appear in a tracked file. Put your own
# vault names, course codes or document prefixes here, for example:
#
#   NP_PRIVACY_PATTERNS=my-vault,PSY\d{4},[A-Z]{3}_\d+
#
NP_PRIVACY_PATTERNS=
